ed, exit qtr)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":3.6,"yoy":-93.9}]}},"profile":{"entities":"","mgmt":"","subseg":"","themes":""},"qtr":"","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"11.1%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"11.8%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.4x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"3.5x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"50.8"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"0.0"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"2.6%"}],"s":"TOTAL","sec":"Services","sec2":"Services","sections":{"business":[{"body":"- Core franchise is LCL cargo consolidation: the deck says the company \"Consolidates shipments for more than 1,100 destinations worldwide through its network across 89 countries\".\n- Network control is promoter-led and described as exclusive: the MD, Mr Pradhan, \"Led formation of exclusive networks\" and is Chairman of both - CP World Global Network (formed with Ken Chiang of Singapore in 2005) and iCargo Alliance (formed in 2011 with CP World Group and Fang Cheng, China).\n- The CP World / iCargo slide describes the network as \"180+ agents connecting 1,100 locations in 89 countries\", an \"Exclusive cargo alliance across 89 countries with 166 offices\", registered in Hong Kong and promoted by CP World Group and Eurasia Group, with main trans-shipment hubs at Singapore, Hong Kong, Busan and Jebel Ali and \"Staff of 1,250 personnel\".\n- Carrier relationships cited as a durable asset: \"Long-standing tie-ups with leading shipping lines like CMA-CGM, Maersk, MSC, ONE, Hapag Lloyd, Hyundai & Cosco, etc.\"\n- Geographic emphasis: \"Strong geographies apart from India, are CIS countries, Africa & Afghanistan\", with network reach into Gulf states plus growing EXIM hubs such as S.E. Asia and South America.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Awards] \"LCL Consolidator of the Year - Exim Star Awards 2025\" and \"LCL Consolidator - 12th Samudra Manthan Awards\".\n- [Execution] Cited execution milestones include a project cargo execution of 3,500 CBMs (India-Indonesia) with multi-stage project handling, and ODC & heavy-lift execution in Bangladesh.\n- [Leadership depth] Promoter-led with long tenures: MD Makarand P. Pradhan, director since 1994, 40+ years in freight forwarding and President of the Consolidators Association of India; CFO Shrikant D. Nibandhe, associated since 1998 and Treasurer of the Consolidators Association of India since its inception in 2003; Promoter-Director Sanjiv A. Potnis with 30+ years; CEO Kaushal Buch with almost 30 years at TTSL.\n- [Sector context] The MD notes the Indian logistics sector benefits from expanding trade, supply-chain diversification and infrastructure investment, \"although geopolitical developments have resulted in periodic disruptions across global shipping routes\".\n- [Extraction gap] The 'Drivers of Growth', 'Marquee Clients', 'Future Strategy', 'Milestones' and 'Abhilaya Operating Snapshot' slides came through as titles only, so no strategy, client-name or milestone content could be read - this is a lost-content gap, not evidence the company omitted them.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 07-08-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"The deck positions Total Transport Systems Limited as an asset-light, multimodal freight forwarder built around LCL cargo consolidation, whose moat is a promoter-chaired exclusive global agent network (CP World Global Network and iCargo Alliance) reaching 1,100+ destinations across 89 countries, extended domestically by the 'Abhilaya' last-mile delivery brand.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.51,"fy":"FY21","mcap":62,"opm":1.0,"pe":null,"roe":-1.7},{"de":0.49,"fy":"FY22","mcap":102,"opm":2.9,"pe":11.1,"roe":18.2},{"de":0.22,"fy":"FY23","mcap":200,"opm":2.5,"pe":38.5,"roe":8.1},{"de":0.44,"fy":"FY24","mcap":185,"opm":2.2,"pe":154.2,"roe":1.7},{"de":0.44,"fy":"FY25","mcap":108,"opm":2.6,"pe":12.1,"roe":11.1}],"